roservice platform adds support for 11+ programming languages","url":"https://hook.io/blog/new-multi-language-support","score":7,"flags":0,"comment_count":3,"description":"\u003cp\u003eIf anyone has any questions about the software please let me know and I'll do my best to answer.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"If anyone has any questions about the software please let me know and I'll do my best to answer.","submitter_user":"marak","user_is_author":true,"tags":["programming","release"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/puyttf","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/puyttf/hook_io_open_source_microservice"},{"short_id":"8ztbbj","created_at":"2015-09-28T16:55:43.000-05:00","title":"Logswan - Fast Web log analyzer using probabilistic data structures","url":"https://github.com/fcambus/logswan","score":12,"flags":0,"comment_count":7,"description":"\u003cp\u003eLogswan is a fast Web log analyzer using probabilistic data structures. It is targeted at very large log files, typically APIs logs. It has constant memory usage regardless of the log file size, and takes approximatively 4MB of RAM.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnique visitors counting is performed using two HyperLogLog counters (one for IPv4, and another one for IPv6), providing a relative accuracy of 0.10%.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProject design goals include : speed, memory-usage efficiency, and keeping the code as simple as possible.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Logswan is a fast Web log analyzer using probabilistic data structures. It is targeted at very large log files, typically APIs logs. It has constant memory usage regardless of the log file size, and takes approximatively 4MB of RAM.\r\n\r\nUnique visitors counting is performed using two HyperLogLog counters (one for IPv4, and another one for IPv6), providing a relative accuracy of 0.10%.\r\n\r\nProject design goals include : speed, memory-usage efficiency, and keeping the code as simple as possible.","submitter_user":"fcambus","user_is_author":true,"tags":["c","release","show"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/8ztbbj","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/8ztbbj/logswan_fast_web_log_analyzer_using"},{"short_id":"zmmcn9","created_at":"2015-09-28T15:30:37.000-05:00","title":"Ad Blockers and the Naked Emperor","url":"http://www.ocsmag.com/2015/09/28/ad-blockers-and-the-naked-emperor/","score":3,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"nogweii","user_is_author":false,"tags":["culture","practices","privacy"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/zmmcn9","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/zmmcn9/ad_blockers_naked_emperor"},{"short_id":"ynxjjh","created_at":"2015-09-28T14:35:26.000-05:00","title":"nil vs None","url":"http://blog.carlosgaldino.com/2015/09/28/nil-vs-none.html","score":6,"flags":1,"comment_count":16,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"carlosgaldino","user_is_author":true,"tags":["programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/ynxjjh","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/ynxjjh/nil_vs_none"},{"short_id":"uabshq","created_at":"2015-09-28T14:23:57.000-05:00","title":"Otto, the successor to Vagrant","url":"https://www.hashicorp.com/blog/otto.html","score":22,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"jpadilla","user_is_author":false,"tags":["devops"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/uabshq","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/uabshq/otto_successor_vagrant"},{"short_id":"syaclz","created_at":"2015-09-28T12:14:03.000-05:00","title":"What are you listening to this week?","url":"","score":5,"flags":1,"comment_count":7,"description":"\u003cp\u003eThere was a thread like this two weeks ago, so I thought I'd repost the same question since it's been a while.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"There was a thread like this two weeks ago, so I thought I'd repost the same question since it's been a while.","submitter_user":"zg","user_is_author":true,"tags":["ask"],"short_id_url":"https://l